    "what": "Marathi/Hindi/English terms mapped to the 15 issue topics the Issue Tracker uses.",
    "why": "39% of Maharashtra posts (561 of 1442) carried analysis.topic = null, because the LLM returned campaign_topic 'None' and it was stored as null. Those posts are invisible to the Issue Tracker and to section 2 of every report. This lexicon assigns a topic deterministically where the text plainly states one.",
    "rules": [
      "Only fills a NULL topic. An LLM-assigned topic is never overwritten - the model reading the sentence beats a word list.",
      "Longest term wins, so a compound ('शेतकरी आत्महत्या') is never split by a shorter one ('शेतकरी').",
      "Terms must be unambiguous for the topic. Anything that could sit under two topics is left out rather than guessed.",
      "Devanagari terms carry no word boundaries in matching, so very short terms are excluded - they match inside unrelated words."
    ],
